WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.204 --> 00:00:24.466
"What?" Riley gasped at Delaney's news. "Jordan said the Blue Demons were expanding the junior division this year!"

2
00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:33.880
"That was the original plan," Delaney replied with a sigh. "But unfortunately, we don't have the funds for it anymore.

3
00:00:33.881 --> 00:00:41.537
Don't worry, Riley. I'm sure you'll make the team. You're a good rider—and Jordan Clark's sister!"

4
00:00:41.538 --> 00:00:49.198
Riley wished she felt as sure as Delaney sounded. At the starting line, she snapped on her helmet.

5
00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:54.783
Then she eyed the track, trying to will the knots in her stomach to go away.

6
00:00:54.784 --> 00:01:01.099
Thinking about Jordan's accident had unsettled her, and Delaney's bad news didn't help one bit.

7
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.359
Especially after watching Quinn, her new competition, ride the track.

8
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:12.174
"Where your brain goes, your body will follow," she whispered to herself.

9
00:01:12.175 --> 00:01:19.911
Three more riders were ahead of Riley in line. Riley kept her eyes on the track, going over it again and again.

10
00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:27.912
It wasn't the toughest track she'd ever seen. But there were definitely tricky spots that would require serious focus.

11
00:01:27.913 --> 00:01:31.249
Riley heard another whistle.

12
00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:40.101
"That's for you, Riley!" Delaney called. "Three, two, one, go!"

13
00:01:40.101 --> 00:01:42.072
Riley pushed off.

14
00:01:42.073 --> 00:01:50.555
The dirt on the track was freshly dug—soft, but not too soft because the riders before Riley had already packed it down in places.

15
00:01:50.556 --> 00:01:55.808
The sun felt warm on her shoulders as she pumped the bike pedals.

16
00:01:55.809 --> 00:02:03.721
She needed to pick up speed and pick it up fast. A steady speed of 13 miles per hour was the goal.

17
00:02:03.722 --> 00:02:08.792
Riley pumped harder, letting her mind go into the "zone."

18
00:02:08.793 --> 00:02:16.801
In seconds the sounds of people and other bikes faded away, and all she could hear were her own tires traveling along the dirt.

19
00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:19.532
The first jump was coming up.

20
00:02:19.533 --> 00:02:25.966
Jumping a bike was a basic skill, one of the first things Riley had learned when she started mountain biking.

21
00:02:25.967 --> 00:02:33.872
Beginning riders, and people who didn't know anything about the sport, thought jumps were rock-star moves—dazzling tricks.

22
00:02:33.873 --> 00:02:39.076
Jumps weren't easy, but a good one was simply about timing and balance.

23
00:02:39.077 --> 00:02:45.774
Riders had to know their bikes, and know when and how to use their bodies to push the bike through the air.

24
00:02:45.775 --> 00:02:53.099
Jumping was definitely Riley's favorite part of the sport. It came naturally to her, like breathing.

25
00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:56.467
Riley pushed herself to pedal harder.

26
00:02:56.468 --> 00:03:03.404
She needed enough speed so she could stop pedaling, pull up the bike, and lift out of the seat at the right moment.

27
00:03:03.405 --> 00:03:07.325
Without enough speed, she wouldn't even get off the ground.

28
00:03:07.326 --> 00:03:12.096
The steps ran through her mind. "Keep your weight between the wheels.

29
00:03:12.097 --> 00:03:16.739
Lower your chest. Feel the force of the jump through your tires."

30
00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:26.068
She felt the front wheel hit the incline of the jump. Then she rose out of the seat, half-standing on the pedals.

31
00:03:26.069 --> 00:03:33.150
The bike's wheels lifted off the ground, and for a perfect moment, time stopped.

32
00:03:33.151 --> 00:03:40.713
Riley held her bike beneath her, suspended in space, the air cool and fresh on her face.

33
00:03:40.714 --> 00:03:45.217
As the bike began to drop, Riley turned her attention to the landing.

34
00:03:45.218 --> 00:03:55.289
The trick to a good landing was keeping the wheels level so they hit the ground at the same time—none of those fancy trick "wheelie" moves that flashy riders liked.

35
00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:59.978
They were a dangerous way to land and would cut into a rider's speed.

36
00:03:59.979 --> 00:04:04.451
Riley braced her arms and legs to absorb the force of the impact.

37
00:04:04.452 --> 00:04:07.608
Bam! A perfect landing!

38
00:04:07.609 --> 00:04:11.204
Riley headed for the straightaway and the second jump.

39
00:04:11.205 --> 00:04:17.607
She glanced at her speedometer: ten miles per hour. She needed more speed.

40
00:04:17.608 --> 00:04:22.606
The next jump was just past a bend in the track, making the timing tricky.

41
00:04:22.607 --> 00:04:27.107
Riley started assessing whether she'd have to slow down on the curve.

42
00:04:27.108 --> 00:04:31.186
An image of Quinn and her flashy bike popped into her head.

43
00:04:31.187 --> 00:04:36.669
Riley would show that stuck-up new girl how good Riley's battered old bike was!

44
00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:44.517
Riley sailed into the jump. But this time her front wheel wobbled as she started to rise.

45
00:04:44.518 --> 00:04:51.667
Riley frantically tried to adjust her weight, to level out her wheels before they hit the ground.

46
00:04:51.668 --> 00:04:53.184
Too late.

47
00:04:53.185 --> 00:04:58.167
The back wheel hit the ground first and slid sideways.

48
00:04:58.168 --> 00:05:04.151
Then Riley came down hard, coughing and tasting dirt.

49
00:05:04.152 --> 00:05:12.405
Riley lay there, her heart racing. A sharp pain shot through her right foot and ankle.

50
00:05:12.406 --> 00:05:17.632
All she could think of was Jordan lying on that stretcher at the Hawk Mountain track.

51
00:05:17.633 --> 00:05:20.844
"Oh no," she murmured.

52
00:05:20.845 --> 00:05:29.979
"Riley!" By now Delaney and Sofia, another member of the Blue Demons, were running toward her.

53
00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:34.031
Sofia bent over Riley. "Are you okay?"

54
00:05:34.032 --> 00:05:44.149
"I . . ." Slowly Riley raised her head and blinked. "My ankle hurts," she said, trying to keep panic out of her voice.

55
00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:47.878
"Did I break anything? Am I okay?"

56
00:05:47.879 --> 00:05:54.361
"We're going to check you out," Delaney said calmly. "Lie still for a second."

57
00:05:54.362 --> 00:05:58.937
He pulled off her bike shoe and examined her foot.

58
00:05:58.938 --> 00:06:07.764
"Ow!" Riley said as Delaney gently moved her ankle around. "It hurts, but I can move it."

59
00:06:07.765 --> 00:06:16.773
"I don't think you've broken anything," Delaney said. "You probably have a nasty sprain, though. Let's see if you can get up."

60
00:06:16.774 --> 00:06:23.853
Slowly Riley hobbled to her feet, clutching Delaney and Sofia's arms for support.

61
00:06:23.854 --> 00:06:31.071
She was a mess, with dirt and grass all over her clothing, but her ankle was actually starting to feel better.

62
00:06:31.072 --> 00:06:38.497
She looked at the track marks in the dirt. "I think I dug another path out of the trail with that fall."

63
00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:47.242
"I'll be sure to put up a Caution sign," Delaney replied with a smile. "Let's see if you can put any weight on that ankle."

64
00:06:47.243 --> 00:06:55.656
Riley gingerly put her foot down. "Not so bad," she said through gritted teeth.

65
00:06:55.657 --> 00:07:04.976
Delaney and Sofia helped her to the sidelines and sat her on the grass under a tree.

66
00:07:04.977 --> 00:07:12.723
Sofia wrapped Riley's ankle with a bandage from the team's first aid kit.

67
00:07:12.724 --> 00:07:20.135
"You're going to have some epic bruises, Riley. You'd better get an x-ray, to be on the safe side."

68
00:07:20.136 --> 00:07:25.299
She went to find Coach Adams while Delaney called Riley's mom.

69
00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:31.870
"Your mom is on her way," Delaney said, sliding his phone back into his pocket.

70
00:07:31.871 --> 00:07:38.781
"Okay." Riley's cheeks burned with embarrassment when she saw a bunch of kids looking at her.

71
00:07:38.782 --> 00:07:48.513
"Nothing to see here!" she called out, forcing a laugh. "I'm fine. You can move along, people!"

72
00:07:48.514 --> 00:07:54.768
Then she lay back and closed her eyes, hoping she'd sounded as light as she'd intended.

73
00:07:54.769 --> 00:08:03.141
"What a disaster," she thought miserably.
